# Project rules for AI assistants (Cursor, etc.)

Read docs/DESIGN.md first: it holds the full pipeline design, decisions, and current status.

## What this is

A single-user tool that drafts LinkedIn posts from work notes and publishes the ones the
owner approves, on a weekly schedule. Human-in-the-loop by design.

## Non-negotiables

- Official LinkedIn API only. Never scrape or browser-automate LinkedIn.
- Nothing publishes without human approval. The weekly job only drafts and notifies.
- Posts use only what is in the logs. Never invent achievements or metrics.
- Secrets live in the gitignored .env. Never commit .env, tokens.json, or state.json.
  Do not run `git add .` or `git add -A`; stage named files only.
- Never run destructive git commands (force-push, hard reset, rebase) without being asked.

## Conventions

- Python 3.10+. Package layout under linkedin_blogger/; run via `python blogger.py <cmd>`
  or `python -m linkedin_blogger`.
- config.py reads everything from .env; BASE_DIR is the repo root (data files live there).
- Keep functions small and focused. Comments explain why, not what.
- No em dashes in prose or comments; straight quotes; no emoji.
- When adding behavior, add or update the relevant docs/DESIGN.md status line.

## Current status

See docs/DESIGN.md "Build status". Working: login, activity fetch, basic draft/approve/
publish. Working: ingest (Stage A step 2), Processing (Stage B), Deliverable queue
(Stage C). Pipeline complete for v1.
